From 4a24be5d85d6ce8e2efefcdc0bdfe326bf09c38a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:44:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] attribute links checks by board reason and strict
 source work

Why: the retained 1.806% sync.links window cannot distinguish strict source publications from background builds or identify which board inputs invalidated the skip. Add bounded passive reason/component counters, per-board inclusive CPU, separate fingerprint/projection/ledger slicing CPU, and start/end in-flight brackets. No cache policy, TTL, schema or configuration change.

Proof: new counter assertions RED on base (12 failed, 1 passed); focused GREEN 78 tests in five files; full scripts/check passes after staging all seven files. Real SQLite same-profile membership insertion, required-read failure/age retry, one-read pass reuse and concurrent strict/background ownership covered. Broad consumer smoke and exact-head CI are separate receipts. Live performance is not accepted by these tests; the historical 1.806% miss remains failed pending one natural-deployment window.
